<title>UK: FORECAST - Consensus on UK company results.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Consensus on UK company results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts' estimates of UK company</p>
<p>results expected in week ending November 1 include -</p>
<p>COMPANY----------------PFT/DIV/EPS--CONSENSUS----RANGE-------PVS</p>
<p>TUESDAY, October 29</p>
<p>Thames Water	  I	PFT	 182.0   177.0-188.0   165.0</p>
<p>Plc				DIV	  10.9    10.3-11.5	9.2</p>
<p>WEDNESDAY, October 30</p>
<p>BAT Industries     Q3	PFT	 690.0   650.0-725.0   659.0</p>
<p>J Sainsbury	  I	 PFT	 390.0   383.0-396.0   451.0</p>
<p>				   DIV	   3.5     3.4-3.5	 3.4</p>
<p>THURSDAY, October 31</p>
<p>Royal Dutch	  Q3	**    1,206.0	1,152-1,280  1,163</p>
<p>Shell Group</p>
<p>Pilkington	   I	 PFT	77.6	 75.0-79.0   104.0</p>
<p>Plc		   DIV	1.75	 1.75-1.95    1.75</p>
<p>Body Shop	    I	 PFT	 n/a	 11.0-11.5     9.1</p>
<p>International</p>
<p>FRIDAY, November 1</p>
<p>- No major companies reporting</p>
<p>NOTES</p>
<p>** The figures for Royal Dutch Shell are for current cost</p>
<p>net earnings.</p>
<p>All profit figures are pretax, exclude exceptional items</p>
<p>unless otherwise stated and are in millions stg. Dividends</p>
<p>are total net and quoted as pence per share.</p>
<p>			     ----oOo----</p>
<p>John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
